<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114702" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστο-μάθεια</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>desire of learning,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				44.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>book containing a summary of useful knowledge</i> or <i>select
				passages,</i> e.g. the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ.
			γραμματική</span> of <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
			</span></i> and the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστομάθειαι</span> of <i><span class="en">
				Hellad.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.2
			</span></i>, al.; so in pl. of the epitome of Strabo; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ -μαθίας</span> (sic) <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				227.53
			</span></i>, Orus in <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				685.57
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
